---
import CommercialLayout from '../../layouts/CommercialLayout.astro';
import BriefForm from '../../components/services/BriefForm.astro';
---

<CommercialLayout
  title="Workflow Care"
  description="Bounded checks, synthetic tests, evidence reports, and corrective time for one accepted registered workflow at $500 per month."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="commercial-shell page-intro__grid">
      <div>
        <h1 class="commercial-title">
          Keep one accepted workflow checkable.
        </h1><p>
          Workflow Care is $500 per month for one registered workflow. It
          records what success means, what can be checked safely, where an alert
          belongs, and who owns recovery.
        </p><div class="commercial-actions">
          <a
            class="commercial-action"
            href="/brief/?source=workflow-care&service=care"
            >Check Care eligibility</a
          ><a class="commercial-action commercial-action--text" href="/care/"
            >Need broader system care?</a>
        </div>
      </div><p class="page-intro__note">
        Initial capacity<br /><strong
          >3 registered Care workflows globally</strong
        ><br />Enrollment follows acceptance and safe-check review.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="commercial-section commercial-section--ink">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>The register defines the promise.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          This example is illustrative. The delivered register uses the client’s
          accepted result and authorized test boundary.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="offer-ledger">
        <div class="offer-row">
          <h3>Workflow ID</h3><p class="offer-price">TT-WF-004</p><p>
            Website inquiry → validated intake record → assigned notification.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="offer-row">
          <h3>Success</h3><p>Durable reference returned</p><p>
            One committed record for one submission ID; authorized destination
            receives the expected alert.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="offer-row">
          <h3>Checks</h3><p>Daily + weekly</p><p>
            Daily read-only state checks where the system supports them. Weekly
            authorized synthetic end-to-end submission.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="offer-row">
          <h3>Recovery</h3><p>Scoped correction</p><p>
            Evidence identifies the failing boundary. Recovery responsibility
            and access are named in the register.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>Included each month.</h2><p class="commercial-section__intro">
          The allowance is intentionally small. It keeps a known workflow
          healthy without turning Care into an open development retainer.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="boundary-list">
        <div>
          <h3>Scheduled checks</h3><p>
            Daily read-only checks where supported and weekly authorized
            synthetic end-to-end checks.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Evidence report</h3><p>
            Current check state, last synthetic result, observed exceptions, and
            any action taken.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>60 minutes aggregate work</h3><p>
            Human corrective or change work per registered workflow, including
            at most one small change of 30 minutes or less.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Small change boundary</h3><p>
            One already-understood adjustment within the registered systems and
            acceptance test. Time does not roll over. Larger or additional
            changes are quoted separately.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>Care is evidence, not constant surveillance.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          There is no 24/7 human response, uptime SLA, emergency promise, or
          guarantee that every live customer inquiry is delivered. Response and
          restoration targets appear only in a written register after the actual
          workflow and operating queue support them. Cancellation includes the
          current register and available evidence handoff; the written agreement
          controls billing dates.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="commercial-shell">
    <BriefForm
      service="care"
      source="workflow-care"
      context="Workflow Care eligibility"
      heading="Check Care eligibility"
    />
  </div>
</CommercialLayout>
